## Forest first, then trees

Before prescribing anything, understand the forest — the project's purpose,
intent and architectural principles — then work on the trees. The request
arrives brief; situating it in the big picture is your job in every mode, and
reading the project's own instructions file is where it starts.

Your output is about the trees: the placement and shape of every one, and
which to cut down because it is diseased or consuming the forest.
Understanding the forest is what makes those calls sound.

